{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The proof cites a nonexistent kinematic lemma. Differentiate the proved Ampère equation instead, commute the time and spatial derivatives, use the time derivative of the magnetic-field matrix (Faraday’s law), and then substitute Gauss’s law.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  have hMaxwell :=\\n    (isExtrema_iff_gauss_ampere_magneticFieldMatrix hA J hJ).mp h\\n  have hGauss : ∀ t x,\\n      (∇ ⬝ (A.electricField 𝓕.c t)) x =\\n        𝓕.ε₀⁻¹ * J.chargeDensity 𝓕.c t x := by\\n    intro t x\\n    rw [(hMaxwell t x).1]\\n    simp [div_eq_mul_inv, mul_comm]\\n  simp_rw [time_deriv_electricField_of_isExtrema hA J hJ h]\\n  simp only [Time.deriv, Space.deriv]\\n  simp (disch := fun_prop)\\n    [fderiv_fun_sub, fderiv_const_mul, fderiv_fun_sum,\\n      time_deriv_space_deriv_commute, time_deriv_magneticFieldMatrix]\\n  simp_rw [hGauss]\\n  simp (disch := fun_prop)\\n    [fderiv_fun_sub, fderiv_const_mul, fderiv_fun_sum,\\n      Space.deriv_commute]\\n  simp only [FreeSpace.c_sq]\\n  field_simp\\n  ring\"}"}}
